\title{No claim of convergence}
\taxon{Remark}
\date{2023-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{We fix #{N}, then take #{x \to x_0}; #{N \not\to \infty}. We make no claim of convergence: this #{\sum^\infty} is just notation. Instead we have an infinite number of approximations (each of different #{N}) and the limit #{x \to x_0} is taken in each separately.}
